# Aston Martin V8 Vantage coupe, 1977-1989.
#
# The Vantage version of the AM V8: deep front air dam, blanked grille with two
# Cibie driving lamps, sealed bonnet bulge, flared wheel arches and a boot
# spoiler. 534 built, 342 saloons and 192 Volantes; the coupe is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_V8_Vantage_(1977)
#
# Dimensions 4.667 m (4.700 with bumper overriders) x 1.829 m x 1.327 m,
# wheelbase 2.610 m. From 1983 the BBS wheels and wider arches raise the width to
# 1.892 m; the early car's 1.829 m is modelled.
#
# Shape reference: a US-market 1979 car in side elevation and a 1978 "fliptail"
# car, chassis V8/1 1889/RCAV, in front and rear three-quarter. The US car has a
# flat bonnet without the European Vantage's sealed bulge, so the bulge and the
# grille lamps are taken from the front three-quarter of the 1978 car. The side
# view governs the air dam, arches and roofline; the rear the integral fliptail
# spoiler and twin exhausts.
#
# Colours: grade (c). Orchard Green (ICI 9010) is the photographed 1978 car's
# factory colour; Suffolk Red and Kent Green are named by astonmartins.com on
# period Vantages; black is a documented Aston finish. Weights 3, 3, 2, 2,
# total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 270 km/h. Comfort 68/282, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 68: a wide 2+2 with
# more shoulder room than the DBS. Classes 3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1977 intro, retires staggered 1999-2002 on a
# twenty-two to twenty-five-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-v8-vantage.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-v8-vantage.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-v8-vantage/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the air dam reads as a separate block, the outer headlamp
# bezels project slightly, and the quarter window is more angular than the car's.
# The US side photograph's flat bonnet was not copied; the European sealed bulge
# comes from the front three-quarter. At 128 px the long bonnet, blanked grille,
# flared arches and fliptail spoiler read as a V8 Vantage.

obj=citycar
name=AstonV8Vantage(OrchardGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1977
intro_month=2
retire_year=2002
retire_month=6
speed=270
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=68
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=282

